po"><addressbook><name>FUKUCHI KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKANO YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANRAKU, TSUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASANO, JUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUCHI, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKANO, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>6-Substituted heteroquinolinecarboxylic acid derivatives represented by general formula (1) and addition salts thereof, exhibiting antagonism against excitatory amino acid receptors, particularly AMPA receptor; and processes for the preparation of both. In formula (1) A is a single bond or methylene (CH2); Y is nitrogen  or =CH-; V is a single bond or methylene (CH2); T is hydroxyl, amino, lower alkoxycarbonyl, carboxyl, formyl, or the like; R is nitro, trifluoromethyl, or halogeno; and R&lt;1&gt; is hydroxyl or lower alkoxy.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à des dérivés d'acide hétéroquinolinecarboxylique 6-substitués représentés par la formule générale (1) et aux sels d'addition associés, qui s'avèrent posséder une action antagoniste dirigée contre les récepteurs d'acides aminés excitateurs, et notamment le récepteur d'AMPA. L'invention se rapporte également à des procédés de préparation de ces dérivés et de leurs sels. Dans la formule (1), A est une liaison simple ou méthylène (CH2); Y est azote ou =CH-; V est une liaison simple ou méthylène (CH2); T est hydroxyle, amino, alcoxycarbonyle inférieur, carboxyle, formyle ou analogue; R est nitro, trifluorométhyle ou halogéno; et R&lt;1&gt; est hydroxyle ou alcoxy inférieur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>